.TH "LMM" "1" "Oct 2026" "lmm 2.2.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-mod-copy - Copy a mod (or every mod) from one profile into another


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm mod copy [<mod-id>] --to <profile> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy an installed mod from one profile into another profile of the same game.

.PP
Nothing is downloaded or re-installed: the mod's files are already in the
cache, and the copy records the mod in the destination profile at the same
version. A lock on the mod is carried over, and a mod marked disabled is
copied disabled.

.PP
The source profile is the 'lmm mod' group's -p/--profile (default: the active
profile) and -s/--source names the source the mod comes from. If the
destination is the active profile the mod is deployed to the game directory;
otherwise it is only recorded, and deployed on the next 'lmm profile switch'
or 'lmm deploy'. The destination's own link method is used, so a destination
that differs from the source profile is called out.

.PP
If the destination already lists the mod, a single-mod copy refuses; pass
--replace to overwrite it in place (keeping its load-order position).

.PP
With --all, every mod of the source profile is copied (no mod ID is given).
Mods already listed in the destination are skipped unless --replace is given.
Steam Workshop items are game-global and are never copied. Use --dry-run to
see what would happen without changing anything.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm mod copy abc123 --to experiment
  lmm mod copy abc123 -p default --to experiment --replace
  lmm mod copy --all --to experiment --dry-run


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	copy every mod of the source profile

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print what the copy would do without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for copy

.PP
\fB--replace\fP[=false]
	overwrite a mod the destination already lists

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	destination profile (required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--source\fP=""
	mod source; "local" names an imported mod (default: the source the installed mod carries, else the game's sole configured source; prompts when several are configured)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


